course: dictionary
lesson: 832
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «Ben» can mean different things. Read the words around it to find out which one the writer means. «The camera showed Jamie, and Ben standing right next to him.» Here Ben is a person, a boy's name, short for Benjamin.
explain: With a capital B and a name after it, like «Ben Nevis», Ben is a place. Ben Nevis is a mountain in Scotland, and it is the highest mountain in the UK. In Scotland, a ben is a mountain or high peak, so the clue is the word for a mountain in the name.
explain: Scottish houses long ago had a «but and ben», a small cottage with two rooms. Here ben is the inner room. The clue is that it has a «but» (the outer room) beside it. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then check it by swapping in your meaning.
fact: Ben is a boy's name, short for Benjamin.
fact: In Scotland, a ben is a mountain or high peak. Ben Nevis is the highest mountain in the UK, at 1,345 m.
fact: Big Ben is the famous great bell in the clock tower at the Houses of Parliament in London. People use the name for the tower too.
fact: In old Scottish cottages, the ben was the inner room, as in «but and ben».
fact: A capital letter and a name after it, like Ben Nevis, is a clue that Ben is a name, not a word for a thing.
exercise: In «The camera showed Jamie, and Ben standing right next to him», what is Ben? | A mountain in Scotland | A bell in a clock tower | A room in a cottage | *A boy's name
exercise: Ben Nevis is the highest mountain in the UK. What does ben mean in Scotland? | The inner room of a cottage | A bell | *A mountain or high peak | A boy's name
exercise: «A but and ben» is an old Scottish cottage with two rooms. What is the ben? | The roof | *The inner room | The kitchen garden | The front door
test: «Ben's mum said the tablet needs a rest at night.» What is Ben here? | *A boy's name | A room in a house | A famous bell | A mountain
test: Which is the clue that Ben means a mountain? | *The name Ben Nevis, a place in Scotland | A capital letter at the start | The word mum | The word tablet
exam: In «Big Ben» the famous bell rings from the clock tower in London, what does Ben mean? | *The great bell, and the name is also used for the tower | A high peak in Scotland | A boy's name | The inner room of a cottage
